# Regenerable market-data and fundamentals caches. NOT committed — 172MB of them, and every byte
# is reproducible from Alpaca SIP and SEC XBRL by the backfill scripts. This mirrors the stance
# already taken in .github/workflows/membership-archive.yml: the DATABASE is disposable and the
# irreplaceable data goes in git. Bars are not irreplaceable; point-in-time MEMBERSHIP is, which is
# why data/membership IS tracked.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are small and expensive to rebuild:
#   data/compliance/  — dated Shariah watchlist snapshots; drift is only visible by diffing two
#   data/events/      — the EDGAR spinoff calendar (40 quarterly index sweeps)
#   data/fund-symbols.txt / .json — the 16,325-name ETF exclusion list
#   data/nasdaq-ever-roster.txt   — the survivorship-free NASDAQ roster
data/bars/
data/bars-raw/
data/fundamentals/

# Backtest output. Regenerable by re-running the measure-* scripts, and large. The DURABLE record
# of a result belongs in docs/quant-experiments/ (the preregistration + terminal card) and in
# docs/JOURNAL.md, not in a 13MB pile of run artefacts.
results/*.json
results/*.log
results/per-symbol/
results/experiments/
